  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1117 PM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nSomewhat higher uncertainty exists for the Saturday evening into\nSunday morning period, with another batch of thunderstorms\nadvertised across parts of northeast Oklahoma and into northwest \nArkansas during this time frame in association with a weak front\nin the vicinity of the Kansas border. Showers and storms may\nlinger into the daylight hours Sunday, primarily across far\nnortheast Oklahoma and northwest Arkansas, with hot and dry \nweather prevailing thereafter through at least the early part of \nnext week. Additional heat headlines will likely be needed during\nthis time frame. Breezy conditions on Sunday, Monday and Tuesday \nwill fuel increased fire weather concerns, with the recent rains \nnot being nearly enough to squelch the impact of the ongoing \ndrought. Toward the end of next week, a cold front continues to be\nadvertised in the longer range models, but the timing and strength\nof the front remains in question. If/when it does come through, an\nincrease in shower and thunderstorm potential will accompany it.",
